      <activity id="b65ebacd-df98-5794-bd1a-78d60b3f8854" activityNameId="625b7c8b-bf8b-53a3-8afa-f43956e56093" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed  [545e8d539c]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed by truck, produced by Electrolysis, AEC using electricity from grid
This dataset represents the supply of 1 kilowatt hour of electricity in a residence, by hydrogen conversion in a fuel cell, PEM. The hydrogen is produced by  Electrolysis, AEC, with electricity from grid as feedstock. Electricity conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 45%. LHV [kWh/kg]: 33.33. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Synthesis efficiency [% LHV input]: 0%. Total cap. Input-related [kW]: 2.74. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 0%. Power [kW]: 1.6. Lifetime [years]: 4.88. Annual operation [hours]: 4100. Allocation factor: 0.88. On-site storage loss [%]: 1.26. Use loss [%]: 0.56. For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: 13eafdfa-3a13-3107-841b-7d4ab54cee72
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_13eafdfa-3a13-3107-841b-7d4ab54cee72.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
